 B_notice="<h4>Second topic · Articles, plurals and uncountable nouns (notice)</h4><table class='tbl'><tr><th>Say</th><th>Not</th></tr><tr><td>I need some <b>advice</b>.</td><td>I need an advice. / advices</td></tr><tr><td>She gave me a lot of <b>information</b>.</td><td>many informations</td></tr><tr><td>I like <b>music</b>.</td><td>I like the music. (in general)</td></tr><tr><td><b>a</b> university, <b>an</b> hour</td><td>an university</td></tr></table><p><b>Rule:</b> use <i>a/an</i> for one countable thing mentioned for the first time, <i>the</i> for a specific thing, and no article for plurals and uncountables in general. <i>Advice, information, furniture, news, equipment</i> are uncountable: no <i>a</i>, no plural. <i>A/an</i> depends on the sound, not the letter.</p>",
 B_trap="<p><b>Spanish-speaker trap:</b> Spanish uses the article with general nouns (<i>La vida es difícil, Me gusta la música</i>). English does not: <b>Life is difficult. I like music.</b></p>",
