 B_notice="<h4>Second topic · Prepositions and collocations (notice)</h4><table class='tbl'><tr><th>Say</th><th>Not</th></tr><tr><td>depend <b>on</b></td><td>depend of</td></tr><tr><td>responsible <b>for</b></td><td>responsible of</td></tr><tr><td>take part <b>in</b></td><td>take part at</td></tr><tr><td><b>do</b> research</td><td>make a research</td></tr><tr><td>I <b>agree</b></td><td>I am agree</td></tr></table><p><b>Rule:</b> verbs, adjectives and nouns take specific prepositions, and many words go together as fixed pairs (collocations: <i>reach a conclusion, pose a risk, strike a balance, do research</i>). Learn them as chunks. At advanced level, these small errors are what a rater notices.</p>",
